# Rate Me (Rayt Me) — overview v3.1

Portable **verified professional reputation**, wherever you go. Domain **rate.me**. Not a self-written CV. Not an app where people casually rate you. **Does not count stars. Measures credible evidence.**

Access: in-person QR, NFC tap, shared link, email signature.

## Sign-up

- Name; photo optional but encouraged
- Account type: **professional** or **university student**
- Profession / job title, or university + field of study
- Company + industry (professionals)
- Location: city, country
- Email and phone, each **independently** public or private

## Verification (checkmark is earned)

- Professionals: work-email code + personal email + phone
- Students: personal email + university email
- Tick only after identity, contact, and employment **or** university checks complete

## Discovery (hard split)

| Has the app | No app |
|---|---|
| Opens in-app full card | Opens **rate.me** website |
| Can **rate** | **Cannot rate** |
| Can open **professional snapshot** | **Cannot** open snapshot |
| | CTA: Download the app (iOS / Play) |

The website is a **preview that sells the app**, not a parallel product. Marketing landing may illustrate snapshot/rating; a scanned public profile on the web must not.

## Card, snapshot, nav

Card: name + tick, title, company · industry, location, score (circular badge), verified reputation, privacy-aware contacts, **Rate** + **Add to my List**, snapshot link (in-app). Phone: hidden or **Request phone**.

Snapshot: short fields (employment, education, skills, languages, licenses, **certifications**, memberships). **CV is supplementary**, never the profile. App tabs: **Browse** · **My List** · **Settings**.

Voice: calm, institutional. Qatar/GCC data protection. EN/AR.
